<%#
  What is being compared, as a row of removable chips under the filter bar.

    render "shared/compare_chips", categories: @item_categories, items: @series

  **Under the bar, not inside the control.** Four chips are 659px and the Compare cell is 256, so
  inside the field they wrapped to three rows and pushed the chart 120px down the page. Under the
  bar they have 1,120px and sit on one line with room to spare, and the row costs a fixed 34px
  however many there are. Carbon's `MultiSelect` puts a count in the field and not the chips for the
  same reason; Polaris ships `Tag` for a row, and Material calls this a chip *set*.

  **`Comparing:` is not decoration.** The chips are a row away from the control that made them, so
  the relationship is carried by a word as well as by position.

  Links rather than form controls: the row is outside the bar's form -- it has to be, to have the
  width -- and a link needs no JavaScript and no second controller. Each is this page minus that one
  selection.
%>
<% entries = compare_chip_entries(categories, items) %>
<% if entries.any? %>
  <div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
    <span class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-600">Comparing:</span>
    <% entries.each do |chip| %>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-brand-200 bg-brand-50 py-0.5 pl-2 pr-0.5 text-xs text-brand-800">
        <%# The swatch is the line this chip stands for, so the row is the chart's key as well. %>
        <svg width="18" height="8" aria-hidden="true" class="shrink-0">
          <line x1="0" y1="4" x2="18" y2="4" stroke="<%= chip[:colour] %>" stroke-width="2.4"
                <%= tag.attributes("stroke-dasharray": MonthRangeHelper::PLOT_DASH_ARRAYS[chip[:dash]]) %> />
        </svg>
        <span class="max-w-56 truncate"><%= chip[:label] %></span>
        <%= link_to compare_without(chip[:entry]),
              class: "flex size-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-brand-700 hover:bg-brand-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-brand-600",
              aria: {label: "Stop comparing #{chip[:label]}"} do %>
          <i class="bi-x-lg text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <% end %>
      </span>
    <% end %>
    <%# "Clear comparison", not "Clear all": the filter bar has its own "Clear all" and it resets
        the date range too. Two controls with the same word doing different things is the fault the
        row action called "Cancel" had. %>
    <%= link_to "Clear comparison", compare_cleared,
          class: "text-xs font-medium text-brand-700 hover:underline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-brand-600" %>
  </div>
<% end %>
